{
  "name": "appworld_execute",
  "description": "Execute Python code in the persistent official AppWorld shell. Variables persist between calls. The global `apis` object is already available; never import or introspect it. Print results you need to observe. Inspect APIs with apis.api_docs.app_descriptions(), apis.api_docs.api_descriptions(app_name=...), and apis.api_docs.show_api_doc(app_name=..., api_name=...). The shell has a hard execution limit, so batch related API calls into one script, avoid repeated probes, and never use os/sys/inspect/open or runtime internals like __closure__/__dict__/request_tracker. Authenticate an app before calling it: apis.<app>.login(username=<supervisor_email or phone_number>, password=<password from apis.supervisor.show_account_passwords()>); store the returned access_token and reuse it instead of logging in again. Once you have enough information to act, perform the action in the next script and call apis.supervisor.complete_task(); do not over-explore. A final text answer cannot change world state. Only pass an `answer` to complete_task when the task instruction asks a question; for action tasks call complete_task() or complete_task(status='success'). The response includes output and task_completed.",
  "parameters": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "code": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Python code to execute in the AppWorld shell. Batch related statements into one call, and when the task is an action task, include the action and supervisor completion together when possible."
      }
    },
    "required": ["code"],
    "additionalProperties": false
  }
}

